invalid.vue:11:1 lint/nursery/useVueValidDefineEmits ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

  × This defineEmits call declares events with both a type and an argument.
  
     9 │ class Payload {}
    10 │ 
  > 11 │ defineEmits<(e: "notify") => void>({ submit: null });
       │ ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
    12 │ defineEmits(local);
    13 │ defineEmits({ ...local });
  
  i Vue accepts only one of the two, and fails to compile the component when both are present.
  
  i Remove either the type between the angle brackets or the argument.
  
  i This rule belongs to the nursery group, which means it is not yet stable and may change in the future. Visit https://biomejs.dev/linter/#nursery for more information.
  

